--- a/CHANGELOG.rst
+++ b/CHANGELOG.rst
@@ -6,6 +6,15 @@ Changelog
 Unreleased
 ++++++++++
 
+- ``@overload``: Choose the first overload that accepts all the arguments of
+  a call according to the typing rules (e.g. ``type[...]``, unions, ``Literal``
+  and generics) instead of combining all of them. Only if none matches, the
+  results of all overloads are combined.
+- ``@overload``: Use what Python passes at runtime: ``*args`` of an unknown
+  length can pass any number of arguments and tuple, list, set and dict
+  literals (also nested ones and comprehensions) are evaluated precisely.
+- Support for ``Literal[...]``
+
 0.20.1 (2026-10-12)
 +++++++++++++++++++
 
